---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Break the shopping cart" hint="A cart holds a book. Two customers add a pen and a mug while some of the three replicas that store it are unreachable. Choose how many replicas must answer, what has failed, whether a stand-in node may step in, and how conflicting versions are settled. A simple model, not Amazon's code or data.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>. Nothing has failed and a read or write needs <b>A majority, two of three</b> replicas. Both add-to-cart requests work (<b>0</b> of 2 refused), every copy is made (<b>3</b> copies when each write is acknowledged), no read misses an item (<b>0%</b>) and a full read returns <b>book, mug, pen</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Failure</b> to <b>Two replicas are down</b>. A strict majority cannot be reached, so both adds are refused (<b>2</b> of 2) and the cart is still just <b>book</b>. The store has chosen to be correct over being available.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Replicas needed</b> to <b>Just one replica</b>. Now every add is accepted (<b>0</b> of 2 refused), but only <b>1</b> copy exists when the write is acknowledged, and <b>67%</b> of the ways a read could be answered miss an item, because the replicas that missed the updates never got them.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Replicas needed</b> back to <b>A majority, two of three</b> and set <b>Stand-in nodes</b> to <b>Sloppy quorum with hinted handoff</b>. A spare node takes the place of a replica that is unreachable and later hands its copy back. Both adds are accepted (<b>0</b> of 2 refused), <b>2</b> copies exist at acknowledgement, no read misses an item (<b>0%</b>) and the cart is complete.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Failure</b> to <b>A network partition splits them</b> and <b>Conflicts</b> to <b>Last write wins</b>. Both sides accept their add, but the carts have diverged: every read finds conflicting versions (<b>100%</b>), and keeping only the later one drops the pen, so <b>100%</b> of reads miss an item and the cart is <b>book, mug</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Conflicts</b> to <b>The application merges the versions</b>. Every read still finds two versions (<b>100%</b>), but the application combines them, so no read misses an item (<b>0%</b>) and the cart is <b>book, mug, pen</b> again. Nothing was lost, which is what the paper's shopping cart relies on.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg dyn" data-dyn>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Replicas needed <select class="pg-in" data-quorum><option value="all">Wait for all three replicas</option><option value="majority" selected>A majority, two of three</option><option value="one">Just one replica</option></select></label>
      <label>Failure <select class="pg-in" data-failure><option value="none">Nothing has failed</option><option value="oneDown">One replica is down</option><option value="twoDown">Two replicas are down</option><option value="partition">A network partition splits them</option></select></label>
      <label>Stand-in nodes <select class="pg-in" data-hint><option value="off">Strict, only the three replicas</option><option value="on">Sloppy quorum with hinted handoff</option></select></label>
      <label>Writers <select class="pg-in" data-writers><option value="off">One client after another</option><option value="on">Two clients at the same moment</option></select></label>
      <label>Conflicts <select class="pg-in" data-resolution><option value="merge">The application merges the versions</option><option value="lastWriteWins">Last write wins</option></select></label>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Add-to-cart requests refused</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Reads that miss an item</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Reads that find conflicting versions</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Copies when a write is acknowledged</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, invented for teaching and not Amazon data: three replicas, A, B and C, hold a cart with a book, and a spare node E can stand in for one that is unreachable. Customer 1 adds a pen and customer 2 adds a mug. A write is accepted when enough replicas, counting a stand-in, acknowledge it. When the failure heals, a stand-in hands its copy to the replica it replaced, but replicas that never received an update are not repaired. In a partition, replica A and the stand-in are on one side and B and C on the other, so the two customers cannot see each other's change. A read hears from the chosen number of replicas, and the model counts every possible choice of which ones, so each percentage is exact. Real systems are more complicated than this, and the paper gives no such figures.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  import { simulate, type Failure, type Quorum, type Resolution } from '../../models/dynamo.ts';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-dyn]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const PERCENT = 100;
    const ADDS = 2; // the two add-to-cart requests
    const DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = { quorum: 'majority', failure: 'none', hint: 'off', writers: 'off', resolution: 'merge' };
    const select = (key: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(`[data-${key}]`);
    const percent = (share: number) => `${Math.round(PERCENT * share)}%`;

    function draw() {
      const result = simulate({
        quorum: select('quorum').value as Quorum, failure: select('failure').value as Failure, hintedHandoff: select('hint').value === 'on',
        concurrentWriters: select('writers').value === 'on', resolution: select('resolution').value as Resolution,
      });
      const accepted = ADDS - result.rejectedWrites;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${result.rejectedWrites} of ${ADDS}`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = result.rejectedWrites > 0 ? 'customers could not add to their cart' : 'every add was accepted';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = percent(result.staleReadShare);
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = result.staleReadShare > 0 ? `of the ways a read could be answered (it waits for ${result.readQuorum})` : `no read misses an item (it waits for ${result.readQuorum})`;
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = percent(result.conflictShare);
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = result.conflictShare > 0 ? 'the reader gets two versions to settle' : 'every read sees a single version';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = accepted > 0 ? String(result.fewestCopies) : 'none accepted';
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = accepted > 0 ? `the write waits for ${result.writeQuorum}; a stand-in's hinted copy counts` : 'no write was acknowledged';
      const bad = [result.rejectedWrites > 0, result.staleReadShare > 0, false, accepted > 0 && result.fewestCopies < 2];
      ['b1', 'b2', 'b3', 'b4'].forEach((b, i) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-${b}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad[i] ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'));

      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const broken = bad.some(Boolean); out.classList.toggle('bad', broken);
      const cart = result.fullCart.join(', ');
      if (!broken) out.textContent = `The store held up: every add was accepted, no read misses an item and each write has at least two copies. A read of every replica returns ${cart}.`;
      else if (result.rejectedWrites > 0) out.textContent = `${result.rejectedWrites} of ${ADDS} adds were refused, so the store is not always writable here. A read of every replica returns ${cart}. Let a stand-in node take over, or accept fewer replies.`;
      else if (result.staleReadShare > 0) out.textContent = `Writes were accepted, but ${percent(result.staleReadShare)} of the ways a read could be answered miss an item. A read of every replica returns ${cart}. Check how the conflict is settled and whether replicas were repaired.`;
      else out.textContent = `Every add was accepted and no read misses an item, but a write is acknowledged with only ${result.fewestCopies} copy, so one more failure could lose it. A read of every replica returns ${cart}.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      Object.keys(DEFAULTS).forEach((k) => (select(k).value = DEFAULTS[k]));
      draw();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
